# TIP3P water.
#
# Jorgensen W, Chandrasekhar J, Madura J, Impey R, Klein M.
# J Chem Phys. 1983;79:926-935.
#
# Charges only. TIP3P does not polarize, so a region built on this force field
# carries fixed multipoles and no induced dipoles, and it is the force field for
# the nonpolarizable region of an embedding.
#
# The charges are the condensed phase ones the model was fitted with, and give a
# dipole moment of 2.35 D rather than the 1.85 D of a water molecule on its own.
# That enhancement stands in for the polarization which the model leaves out, so
# these charges are not the ones to give a polarizable region: it would then be
# polarized twice.
#
# The Lennard-Jones parameters of the model are not here. This file holds what
# the embedding uses, and the repulsion and dispersion of the environment are
# not part of it.
#
# The sites are the atoms in the order a structure file gives them, the oxygen
# and then the two hydrogens.

@FORCEFIELD
name:  WATER
sites: 3
units: au

@MULTIPOLES
ORDER 0
3
1    -0.834000
2     0.417000
3     0.417000
